    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1084">

                <pb facs="0996" n="984" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg984"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760d.61/368: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-30T20:00:00+03:00">October 30, 1939—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 30—2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>837. I have just been informed that the British broadcast from London at 7 p.m.,
                    Moscow time in reporting the expected departure tomorrow of the Finnish
                    delegation for Moscow stated that a Finnish newspaper this evening had published
                    a report alleging “when Paasikivi was in Moscow a high official of the American
                    Embassy handed him a personal message of sympathy from President Roosevelt
                    asking to be kept informed of the progress of the negotiations.” I need hardly
                    assure the Department that this report, assuming it to have been published in a
                    Finnish newspaper,<anchor n="61" xml:id="d1084-f1"/> is completely without <pb
                        facs="0997" n="985" xml:id="pg985"/> foundation. Neither I nor any member of
                    the Embassy staff saw Paasikivi during his visits to Moscow.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Helsinki.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1084-f1" n="61" xml:id="d1084-f1-content">
                <p>The Minister in Finland had informed the Department in his telegram No. 298,
                    October 30, that the report published in the Finnish press had been reprinted
                    from the Stockholm newspaper <hi rendition="#italic">Social-Demokraten</hi>
                    (760d.61/367).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
